<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>Practicing Whole Proofs By Contradiction</title>

    <p>
        Recall a real number <m>x</m> is <term>rational</term> if
        <m>x=\frac{a}{b}</m> for some <m>a,b\in\mathbb{Z}</m> with
        <m>b\neq 0</m>.
        Otherwise, we say <m>x</m> is <term>irrational</term>.
        Recall that the set of rationals is denoted <m>\mathbb{Q}</m> (for
        quotient).
    </p>

    <p>
        You may use any of the following as lemmas without proof. We will prove <xref ref="lem-sqrt2"/> soon.
    </p>

    <lemma xml:id="lem-sqrt2">
      <statement>
        <p>
           The real number <m>\sqrt{2}</m> is irrational.
  
        </p>
      </statement>
    </lemma>

    <lemma>
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>x,y\in\mathbb{R}</m>, if <m>xy=0</m> then <m>x=0</m> or
        <m>y=0</m>.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </lemma>

<lemma>
  <statement>
    <p>
      For all <m>a,b,x,y\in\mathbb{Z}</m> and <m>n\in\mathbb{N}</m>, if
        <m>a\equiv x \pmod{n}</m> and <m>b\equiv y\pmod{n}</m> then
        <m>ab \equiv xy\pmod{n}</m>.
    </p>
  </statement>
</lemma>


    <activity workspace="5in">
        <p>
            Work to prove the theorems in <xref ref="act-contradictionstart"/>.
        </p>

        <p>
            What are some examples of contradictions you can get?
        </p>
    </activity>
</handout>